# starchart.phext — the chart of future Moonshots

Created 2026-11-24 at Will's direction (main chat,
2026-11-24 15:01 CST): a new phext in exo-plan focused on
future Moonshots.

## Charter

starchart.phext is the chart of future Moonshots —
candidates not yet numbered into moonshots.phext. An entry
here is a sighting, not a commitment: charting something
records that it was seen and judged worth watching; it
promises nothing.

Promotion: a sighting becomes a numbered Moonshot only by
Will's call. On promotion the entry migrates to
moonshots.phext (the register of record, same exo-plan
home) and takes its permanent moonshot number there; this
chart keeps a migration note at the sighting's coordinate.
Numbers are never reused in either register.

## The hop rule — standing (Will, 2026-11-24 15:05 CST)

Will, verbatim: "whenever I list a new star, see if we can
already hop to it. just ship immediately if we can."

So: every new star gets a hop-check on listing — an honest
assessment of whether the star is already reachable with
current assets. If it is, we ship immediately instead of
charting-and-waiting, and the entry records the hop and what
shipped. The star stays charted as the full moonshot
regardless; a hop ships only the reachable rung.

## Entry scheme

Sightings are numbered monotonically from 1, in the order
charted; a sighting number is permanent in this chart.
Each sighting lives at a holographic coordinate computed
once, at inscription, from the sighting's own seed line by
the Singular merge (task_coordinate.py), and stored in
the source.

Source of truth: starchart-source.json beside the builder
(build_starchart_phext.py) in exo-plan. Edit the JSON,
never the .phext; rebuild after every edit.

